# /hm:spec — what, why, and how to verify

`/hm:spec <slug>` turns a task into acceptance criteria; it is the only interview. Write files in English; talk to the user in `{{ config.locale }}`.

{{ hm.cli() }}

{{ hm.choices() }}{{ hm.preflight("spec") }}

## Step 0 — Skip check

Skip the interview only when all five hold: one file or config (docs count, tests do not); acceptance obvious from the title; no API, IPC, schema, file-format, CLI-output or user-facing message change (a typo fix is not one); reversible within an hour with no user impact; no **Boundary** left open (Step 2). A detailed ask is not a small one; when unsure, interview. Then write a minimal SPEC (Intent, one Given-When-Then scenario, Verification), the reason under Refinement Decisions, `irreversible_decisions: []`. Only a non-code change may write `ac: []`; a code change gets one testable AC. Stamp it unasked: `hm spec_machine finalize --slug <slug> --exempt`.

## Step 1 — Prior work

Grep `specs/SPEC-*.md` and `work-docs/PLAN-*.md` for key terms; run `hm memory_retrieve --topic "<topic>"`. Read `work-docs/RESEARCH-<slug>.md` if it exists.

## Step 2 — Interview

**Boundary.** Before the SPEC, read the code the ask touches: which inputs take the new behaviour, which keep the old, and which existing behaviour must stay? The code shows today's behaviour, not which of it the DRI wants kept, so the boundary is open unless the ask states it or the change keeps no existing behaviour. Ask an open boundary in round 1 (one of its 3 questions), recommendation first; a Refinement Decision alone is not enough.
{% if _depth != 'minimal' %}
<!-- @hm:comprehension:brief -->
**Design brief, before round 1:** what research or a prior SPEC settled, the draft ACs, and which categories are open or defaulted (with why). One screen.
{% endif %}
Ask only what the DRI owns: categories 1–4 and each irreversible decision, with {{ hm.ask() }}, at most 3 questions per round; always offer "Other — let me describe". At most {{ _cap }} open-ended follow-up(s) per turn. Settle categories 5–6 and every oracle yourself. Once nothing the DRI owns is open (round 1 included), one question per round offers **"Approve this SPEC and end interview"** and "Approve after spec-validator": the DRI's only approval (silence never counts). Show your Refinement Decisions with the approval question as the change card: write the SPEC and its yaml (Steps 3–3.5) first, then ask it with `hm change_card spec --slug <slug>`'s output as your message, verbatim{% if config.locale != 'en' %} (its free-text lines in `{{ config.locale }}`){% endif %}, rerun after any SPEC edit (the validator's too, before the stamp); add no other summary: the DRI approves from it, the SPEC file is reference. Stop when the DRI approves or after `interview.main_loop.max_rounds` ({{ _rounds if _rounds else 'unlimited' }}) rounds.

Categories: 1. **Intent** (why now); 2. **Outcomes** ("done", observably); 3. **In-scope scenarios** (2–4 Given-When-Then: normal, edge, failure); 4. **Non-goals**; 5. **Constraints** (the test framework is mandatory); 6. **Verification** (each scenario → unit, integration or manual).

**Oracle, for every AC.** Choose `oracle_source` (golden, differential, property, rubric or consensus; a property also needs `input_domain`, `transformation`, `expected_relation`) and write `oracle_evidence`: why it is independent of the code. "The test will check it" is circular.

**Irreversible decisions** (not cheaply undone): `category` is exactly one of {{ hm.irr_categories() }}. Each is `{id: IRR-NNN, decision, category, rationale, source: spec}`; `irreversible_decisions: []` is valid.

{% if _depth != 'minimal' %}
<!-- @hm:comprehension:round_state -->
**Round state.** Open each round after the first with `## Interview Round {N}`, the decisions locked so far, the delta since the last round, and what this round resolves.
{% endif %}
{%- if _depth == 'deep' %}
<!-- @hm:comprehension:decision_depth -->
**Per-question envelope.** For each question: what it decides, which sections each option rewrites, your recommended option and why, and what undoing it later costs (minutes, a phase, a migration).

<!-- @hm:comprehension:teach_back -->
**Closing readback.** The change card is the readback; add no restatement.
{% endif %}
## Step 3 — Write the SPEC

Write `specs/SPEC-<slug>.md`. Frontmatter: `type: spec`, `task_slug`, `status`, `created`, `tags`, `test_framework`, `interview_rounds`, `summary`. Sections: Intent; Outcomes; In-Scope Scenarios (S1…); Non-Goals; Constraints (table); Irreversible Decisions (table, or "none"); Acceptance Criteria, each `### AC-NNN: <title>`; Verification (scenario, mode, AC); Open Questions; Refinement Decisions. Open Questions holds only what the DRI must decide. Refinement Decisions lists each choice you made for the DRI: what, why and the cost to undo. {{ hm.edit_in_place() }}

## Step 3.5 — Write the machine.yaml

`specs/SPEC-<slug>.machine.yaml`:
```yaml
schema_version: 3
spec_slug: <slug>
verification_tier: 1
irreversible_decisions: []
ac:
  - id: AC-001
    title: <the heading's title>
    type: mechanical   # parametric | property | judgment
    executable_predicate: <python expression>    # mechanical
    golden_table: [{input: {}, expected: null}]  # parametric
    rubric_id: <id>    # judgment, + judgment_subject_paths
    pending_test: true
    oracle_source: golden
    oracle_evidence: <why it is independent>
```

A behaviour-unchanged AC covers only what no existing test asserts; it is parametric, its golden rows computed at spec time by running the unchanged code and never regenerated. A raising case is a mechanical AC (`pytest.raises`), not a golden row. `/hm:execute` writes each testable AC's test.

## Step 4 — Check

Run `hm spec_machine finalize --slug <slug> --strictness {{ _strict }}` (a check; writes nothing). On exit 1, fix and rerun once; if it still fails, report and stop.

## Step 4.5 — Quality score

Read its `quality`.{% if _strict == 'block' %} `blocked: true` halts: give each `weak_dimensions` entry a fix and leave `status: draft`.{% else %} A low score only warns: print `weak_dimensions` and continue.{% endif %}

## Step 4.6 — spec-validator

One advisory pass, only on Step 4's `"validator": "run"` or "Approve after spec-validator": {{ hm.dispatch("spec-validator", "with the SPEC, its yaml and any RESEARCH doc") }}. Settle what you can under Refinement Decisions as a default; surface every critical critique before any stamp; an irreversible-decision critique is never a default, it goes to `irreversible_decisions`; Open Questions takes an oracle with no independent source and any WHY, WHAT, scope or trade-off.

## Step 5 — Status and stamp

With Open Questions empty: if the DRI chose "Approve this SPEC and end interview", or the validator one with no critical critique, run `hm spec_machine finalize --slug <slug> --strictness {{ _strict }} --approve`; else `--exempt` only when `irreversible_decisions: []` and the DRI was not asked (`auto_full`). Either re-checks, stamps and sets `status: approved`; on exit 1 nothing is stamped. Else leave `status: draft`, unstamped.

Print the SPEC path, status and approval, then STOP. `/hm:execute <slug>` is the user's call; if the world model began this run, enter it now unless its Advance rule stops.
